    translation: Mereka tidak akan bermain malam ini.
  - id: SF-N03
    section: 1
    sentence: I-will-not-be-late
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Saya tidak akan terlambat.
  - id: SF-N04
    section: 1
    sentence: We-will-not-buy-it
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Kami tidak akan membelinya.
  - id: SF-N05
    section: 1
    sentence: He-will-not-call-you
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Dia (laki-laki) tidak akan meneleponmu.
  - id: SF-Q01
    section: 2
    sentence: Will-you-help-me?
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Apakah kamu akan membantuku?
  - id: SF-Q02
    section: 2
    sentence: Will-she-join-us?
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Apakah dia (perempuan) akan bergabung dengan kami?
  - id: SF-Q03
    section: 2
    sentence: Will-they-come-tonight?
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Apakah mereka akan datang malam ini?
  - id: SF-Q04
    section: 2
    sentence: Will-it-rain-tomorrow?
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Apakah besok akan hujan?
  - id: SF-Q05
    section: 2
    sentence: Will-the-train-arrive-soon?
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Apakah kereta akan segera tiba?
  - id: SF-R01
    section: 3
    sentence: I-will-call-you-tonight
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Saya akan meneleponmu malam ini.
  - id: SF-R02
    section: 3
    sentence: They-will-not-come-tomorrow
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Mereka tidak akan datang besok.
  - id: SF-R03
    section: 3
    sentence: Will-he-buy-a-ticket?
    alternativeSentences: 
    translation: Apakah dia (laki-laki) akan membeli tiket?
  tutorials:
  - section: 0
    formula: Subject|will|Verb 1|Object / Keterangan
    explanation: 'Semua subject memakai <b>will</b> + Verb 1.

      Verb setelah
      will selalu bentuk dasar (will call, will go).'
    exampleSentence: She-will-call-you
    exampleRoles: Subject|will|Verb 1|Object
  - section: 1
    formula: Subject|will|not|Verb 1|Object / Keterangan
    explanation: 'Tambahkan <b>not</b> setelah will (will not = won''t).

      Verb
      tetap bentuk dasar (will not forget).'
    exampleSentence: I-will-not-forget
    exampleRoles: Subject|will|not|Verb 1
  - section: 2
    formula: Will|Subject|Verb 1|Object / Keterangan + ?
    explanation: 'Kalimat tanya diawali <b>Will</b>, lalu subject dan Verb 1.

      Kalimat
      diakhiri tanda tanya (?).'
    exampleSentence: Will-he-come-tomorrow?
    exampleRoles: Will|Subject|Verb 1|Keterangan + ?
